<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">Handoff Protocol, Normal Mode</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">The handoff is solid for a few weeks. The capture file is the record. The memory is the standing rule. The two stop-note docs stay untouched until someone decides their scope.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">1. Capture: done, twice. The first run used the scratchpad as cwd and logged nothing. The second passed the workspace cwd and transcript path and logged the session.<br>2. Config: read. Git is off. Two handoff_docs entries are configured.<br>3. Stop-notes: skipped on purpose. Both docs hold <span style="white-space:nowrap">2026-10-12</span> notes for other work, and this chat is outside their scope.<br>4. Memory: done, as above.<br>5. Git: off, nothing done.<br>6. Ready: /clear.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">Shadrian&#x27;s Prompts</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">&quot;ok here is the deal opera is a browser...&quot;</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Too many goals in one message: Opera, Gmail, cloud persistence, a React template, ports, and Supabase. The useful request was buried.<br>Better: &quot;On Ubuntu, a bash command that lists free localhost ports in 4100–4999. Return the first three. One line.&quot;</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">&quot;dont relapse into the react tempalte tho son --- FOcus on protols first&quot;</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">A correction, not a request. The constraint belonged at the top of the prompt.<br>Better: &quot;Answer only: [question]. No templates, no files.&quot;</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">&quot;the next few session will be bash scripts and why you chose that&quot;</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">A project-wide rule. It belongs in memory or CLAUDE.md, not repeated per prompt.<br>Better: State the rule once, then ask questions: &quot;Ubuntu bash first, Python one-line side note.&quot;</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">&quot;ok linux ubunto commands only -- while u keep sidenote how would u do wit wiht python&quot;</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">The same rule, typed a third time. Repeating it means it was never saved as standing context.<br>Better: Save it once. The repeats stop.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">&quot;bro literally no files== super barbone - Also i think iu geneinly messedu the command&quot;</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">A specific error needed the error text. &quot;I messed up the command&quot; with no output gives nothing to debug.<br>Better: Paste the command and the terminal output.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">Rules for prompting Claude Code</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">- Put the goal, format, and constraints in the first line.<br>- One deliverable per prompt. Split unrelated asks.<br>- Name the working directory. The cwd switched to the scratchpad mid-session, which broke the first handoff capture.<br>- Paste error text, not a description of it.<br>- Store standing rules once, in memory or CLAUDE.md, instead of retyping them.<br>- For multi-step work, use plan mode first.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:8px 0 8px 0"><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#1B1F23">Followback Immediately</h2></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">No Notion tool is connected in this session, so the task cannot be created from here. Paste this into Notion:</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">CleanUp Tab Clutter: follow-ups from the <span style="white-space:nowrap">2026-10-13</span> port and handoff session<br>1. Delete claudeOS/handoff/sessions/<span style="white-space:nowrap">2026-10-13</span>_scratchpad_unknown.json. Awaiting your yes.<br>2. Pick the artifact skill type. Nothing started.<br>3. Check Opera Browser Connector port settings and confirm it accepts the three ports you choose.<br>4. Decide the handoff question: capture-only record, or a new handoff doc for this kind of work.<br>5. Save the port finder in the workspace if you want to reuse it.<br>6. Supabase: held. I name the org and wait for your pick first, per the workspace CLAUDE.md.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Already done: the scratchpad .md capture was deleted.</p></td></tr></table></td></tr></table></td></tr>
